Phasmid: font availability

What:     Only font files that publish a family in fonts.families are
          reachable (CSS, fallback, emoji, local(), queryLocalFonts(),
          canvas). At startup the browser writes a fontconfig file, checks
          that it reaches exactly the kept files and exports it as
          FONTCONFIG_FILE to every child. Linux profiles filter the host's
          configuration. Windows profiles use a standalone configuration over
          the Windows font store (--phasmid-windows-fonts, default
          $XDG_DATA_HOME/phasmid/fonts/windows/<build>) with Windows render
          settings, and resolve only listed family names. Missing files are
          logged once and their families stay absent. fonts.default_* become
          the generic family pref defaults.
Why:      Host fonts outside the claimed device's set identify the host, and
          a Windows profile must not resolve Linux families.
Profile:  os.family, fonts.families, fonts.default_sans, fonts.default_serif,
          fonts.default_monospace, fonts.emoji, fonts.ui_font
Hooks:    chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc BasicStartupComplete;
          chrome/browser/ui/prefs/prefs_tab_helper.cc RegisterProfilePrefs;
          components/services/font_data/font_data_service_impl.cc
          MatchFamilyName, LegacyMakeTypeface;
          components/services/font/font_service_app.cc MatchFamilyName;
          GN deps in chrome/BUILD.gn, chrome/app/BUILD.gn,
          chrome/browser/ui/prefs/BUILD.gn,
          components/services/font{,_data}/BUILD.gn
Contexts: main, same- and cross-origin iframe, worker, shared worker, service
          worker, OffscreenCanvas in workers; headless and headful.
Guard:    tests/guards/fonts/availability.py

